l, not allowed.\n- A1-B2: slope (2-1)/(2-1)=1, sunny. So line L_A1_B2: y = x.\n- A1-B3: slope (3-1)/(2-1)=2, sunny. L_A1_B3: y = 2x - 1.\n- A1-C1: slope (1-1)/(3-1)=0, horizontal, not allowed.\n- A1-C2: slope (2-1)/(3-1)=0.5, sunny. L_A1_C2: y = 0.5x + 0.5.\n- A1-D1: slope (1-1)/(4-1)=0, horizontal, not allowed.\n\nThus A1 can be paired with B2, B3, C2.\n\n- Through A2=(1,2) and B1=(2,1): slope (1-2)/(2-1) = -1, not allowed.\n- A2-B2: horizontal, not allowed.\n- A2-B3: slope (3-2)/(2-1) = 1, sunny. L_A2_B3: y = x+1.\n- A2-C1: slope (1-2)/(3-1) = -0.5, sunny. L_A2_C1: y = -0.5x + 2.5? Actually line through (1,2) and (3,1): slope -0.5, equation y - 2 = -0.5(x-1) => y = -0.5x + 2.5.\n- A2-C2: slope (2-2)/(3-1) = 0, horizontal, not allowed.\n- A2-D1: slope (1-2)/(4-1) = -1/3 ≈ -0.333, sunny. L_A2_D1: y = -1/3 x + 7/3? Actually line through (1,2) and (4,1): slope -1/3, equation y - 2 = -1/3 (x-1) => y = -1/3 x + 7/3.\n\nThus A2 can be paired with B3, C1, D1.\n\n- Through A3=(1,3) and B1=(2,1): slope (1-3)/(2-1) = -2, sunny. L_A3_B1: y = -2x + 5.\n- A3-B2: slope (2-3)/(2-1) = -1, not allowed.\n- A3-B3: horizontal, not allowed.\n- A3-C1: slope (1-3)/(3-1) = -1, not allowed.\n- A3-C2: slope (2-3)/(3-1) = -0.5, sunny. L_A3_C2: y = -0.5x + 3.5? Actually line through (1,3) and (3,2): slope -0.5, equation y - 3 = -0.5(x-1) => y = -0.5x + 3.5.\n- A3-D1: slope (1-3)/(4-1) = -2/3 ≈ -0.667, sunny. L_A3_D1: y = -2/3 x + 11/3? Actually line through (1,3) and (4,1): slope -2/3, equation y - 3 = -2/3 (x-1) => y = -2/3 x + 11/3.\n\nThus A3 can be paired with B1, C2, D1.\n\n- Through A4=(1,4) and B1=(2,1): slope (1-4)/(2-1) = -3, sunny. L_A4_B1: y = -3x + 7.\n- A4-B2: slope (2-4)/(2-1) = -2, sunny. L_A4_B2: y = -2x + 6.\n- A4-B3: slope (3-4)/(2-1) = -1, not allowed.\n- A4-C1: slope (1-4)/(3-1) = -3/2 = -1.5, sunny. L_A4_C1: y = -1.5x + 5.5.\n- A4-C2: slope (2-4)/(3-1) = -2/2 = -1, not allowed.\n- A4-D1: slope (1-4)/(4-1) = -3/3 = -1, not allowed.\n\nThus A4 can be paired with B1, B2, C1.